ces between blocks of group algebras. J. Algebra 664, 815–887 (2025)\nL90: \nL91:   3. Bouc, S., Yılmaz, D.: Diagonal \\(p\\)-permutation functors. J. Algebra 556, 1036–1056 (2020)\nL92:   4. Bouc, S., Yılmaz, D.: Diagonal \\(p\\)-permutation functors, semisimplicity, and functorial equivalence of blocks. Adv. Math. 411(part A), 108799 (2022)\nL93: \nL94:   5. Bouc, S., Yılmaz, D.: Stable functorial equivalence of blocks. Pac. J. Math. 328(2), 217–226 (2024)\nL95: \nL96:   6. Broué, M.: Isométries parfaites, types de blocs, catégories dérivées. Astérisque 181–182, 61–92 (1990)\nL97: \nL98:   7. Knörr, R., Robinson, G.R.: Some remarks on a conjecture of Alperin. J. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) 39(1), 48–60 (1989)\nL99:   8. Linckelmann, M.: The Block Theory of Finite Group Algebras, vol. II. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge (2018)\nL100: \nL101:   9. Rickard, J.: Splendid equivalences: derived categories and permutation modules. Proc. Lond. Math. Soc. (3) 72(2), 331–358 (1996)\nL102: \nL103:   10. Thévenaz, J.: \\(G\\)-Algebras and Modular Representation Theory. Clarendon Press, Oxford (1995)\nL104: ## Acknowledgements\nL105: \nL106: The first two authors are very grateful for the hospitality they experienced during their visits at the Mathematics Department at Bilkent University. The third author is supported by the Scientific and Technological Research Council of Türkiye (TÜBİTAK) under the 3501 Career Development Program with Project No. 123F456.\nL107: \nL108: ## Author information\nL109: ### Authors and Affiliations\nL110: \nL111:   1. Department of Mathematics, University of California, Santa Cruz, CA, 95064, USA\nL112: \nL113: Robert Boltje\nL114: \nL115:   2. CNRS-LAMFA, Université de Picardie, 33 rue St Leu, 80039, Amiens, France\nL116: \nL117: Serge Bouc\nL118: \nL119:   3. Department of Mathematics, Bilkent University, 06800, Ankara, Turkey\nL120: \nL121: Deniz Yılmaz\nL122: \nL123: ### Corresponding author\nL124: \nL125: Correspondence to Serge Bouc (serge.b